{swarm_brief}

Apply the full normalisation-and-fingerprinting pipeline to the candidate queries from the Query Parser. Use the historical fingerprint registry below to discard any duplicates. Output a JSON object with keys unique_queries and updated_fingerprints.

Historical fingerprint registry (JSON array, may be empty):
{fingerprints}

with.input:
Incoming goal: ${state.goal}

Produce a Swarm Brief with four sections: SUB-OBJECTIVES, ROLE ASSIGNMENTS, COMMUNICATION PROTOCOL, and CONFLICT RULES that the Commander, Scout, Executor, Validator, and Retry agents will follow.

Expected output: A structured Swarm Brief with exactly four labelled sections: SUB-OBJECTIVES, ROLE ASSIGNMENTS, COMMUNICATION PROTOCOL, and CONFLICT RULES. Each section must be concrete and actionable. If the goal is empty or unrecognisable, return: NO DATA: goal input was empty or unrecognisable.

tasks.description:
Audit every numerical claim, calculation, statistic, ranking, and logical assertion in the browser findings below for internal consistency and accuracy.

Original goal: {goal}

Browser findings (including validation report):
{browser_findings}

Assess the recency and freshness of every fact in the browser findings. Compare dates against today's date.

Browser findings:
{browser_findings}

Apply normalisation, regex whitespace/punctuation stripping, stop-word removal, token sorting, and fingerprint deduplication to the combined findings. Remove any duplicates that slipped through earlier passes.

Combined findings:
{browser_findings}

with.input:
Original goal: ${state.goal}

Swarm Brief:
${outputs.swarm_coordinate.raw}

Findings from primary pass (including validation report):
${outputs.swarm_execute.raw}

Primary pass audit results:
${outputs.advanced_validation.raw}

Findings from retry pass:
${outputs.swarm_retry.raw}

Retry pass audit results:
${outputs.retry_advanced_validation.raw}

Combine all UNIQUE and non-DEDUP-REMOVED findings into a single clear, complete answer. Apply these rules before writing: (1) If the same fact appears in both passes, include it only once, preferring the more detailed version. (2) Merge near-identical statements into a single canonical one. (3) Exclude anything tagged DEDUP-REMOVED or SKIPPED (duplicate query). (4) Footnote anything tagged STALE with: [Note: this data may be outdated]. (5) Flag MATH-FAIL or LOGIC-FAIL items as: [Uncertain: <reason>]. (6) Present only verified information.

Expected output: A clear, structured, fully deduplicated answer combining verified findings from both browsing passes, formatted per the Swarm Brief's output protocol. STALE items are footnoted, uncertain figures are flagged, DEDUP-REMOVED entries are excluded. If the combined findings are still empty or unhelpful, state in plain language that no result could be produced — do not invent figures or estimates.

Original goal: ${state.goal}

Swarm Brief:
${outputs.swarm_coordinate.raw}

Validated findings from the squad:
${outputs.swarm_execute.raw}

Write a clear, structured answer that directly addresses the user's goal using only the information above, formatted per the Swarm Brief's output protocol. Apply these deduplication rules before writing: (1) If the same fact, figure, or data point appears more than once in the findings, include it only once. (2) Merge near-identical statements into a single canonical one. (3) Remove any entry marked SKIPPED (duplicate query). If the findings are empty or unhelpful, say so honestly.

Expected output: A clear, structured, deduplicated answer that directly addresses the user's goal using only the validated browser findings, formatted per the Swarm Brief's communication protocol. If the browser returned no useful data, state in plain language that the sources returned nothing and no result could be produced.

